<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18950" body-key="">
	  <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">β</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βῆτα</span></b> ,
			indecl., second letter of the Gr. alphabet: hence as
		numeral, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">β́</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δύο</span>
			 and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεύτερος,</span> but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">
				b'
			</span>
			=
			<i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				000
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> to represent
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ϝ</span>, freq. in <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, esp. in 
				Lacon.
			 words, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βείκατι,</span>
		etc.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
